{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he counted them.</b> Moses, for he is the principal, and he began with Reuben, for he is the firstborn; after him Simeon, who was born after him; after him Gad, firstborn of Leah's handmaid. Now: the standard of Reuben, then the standard of Judah, then the standard of Ephraim, then the standard of Dan, and those encamped around each standard, as they were at the dedication of the altar. Know that since the tribes were twelve — Levi having departed, and Joseph having two sons, and the directions of the world being four — each direction has three. Now Leah has five sons; remove one and she has two standards. They completed the standard with the firstborn of her handmaid and placed it with the standard of Reuben, for he too is a firstborn. And the second standard is Judah's, with his younger brothers encamped around him. And Rachel has a standard of her own; Ephraim stands in place of Joseph and precedes Manasseh, according to Jacob's word. And the fourth standard belongs to Rachel's handmaid — it is her firstborn; after him Asher, though he is younger in years than Naphtali, because the standard belongs to the son of Rachel's handmaid — this privilege is given to the son of Leah's handmaid. And if you look well, you will know that the head is the south and the tail is the north; I cannot fully explain. Therefore Reuben is in the south, for he is the head, and Dan in the north. Know that none were as mighty among the tribes as the tribe of Judah, compared to a lion's cub, and the tribe of Dan, compared likewise in Moses' words; therefore they were first and last. And he mentioned their census for Reuben and also for Simeon, to indicate the rest, for Scripture took a short path."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:59.017287399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}